{
  "name": "Day 42 Solution: AI Agent Review",
  "description": "One real AI Agent combining Week 6: Simple Memory, a Wikipedia HTTP Request Tool, the Day 39 knowledge base as a vector store tool, an error output, and a rating-based feedback branch.",
  "tags": [
    "week-06",
    "ai-agents",
    "day-42",
    "openai",
    "review",
    "solution"
  ],
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "overview-sticky",
      "name": "Overview Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Day 42 Solution: AI Agent Review\n\nCombines this week's techniques in one real **AI Agent**: OpenAI Chat Model, **Simple Memory** keyed by `conversation_id`, a **Wikipedia Search** HTTP Request Tool, and the Day 39 knowledge base as a **vector store tool**. After the answer, a rating routes low scores to a logging step (Day 40).\n\n**Before testing:** run Day 39's *Load Knowledge Base* once, so the `course_knowledge_base` store has data.\n\n**Error handling:** the AI Agent's Settings use *On Error → Continue (using error output)*, so a failed model or tool call goes to **Build Error Response** instead of crashing the run.\n\n**Credentials needed to run for real:** OpenAI API key (Chat Model and Embeddings).\n\n**Reference:** WEEK_06_AI_AGENTS/DAILY_TASKS/DAY_42_AI_Agent_Review.md",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 460
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "readme-sticky",
      "name": "Readme Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        740,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow Purpose & Architecture\n\nAn EdTech-style support assistant. **Input** (POST body): `request` (string), `conversation_id` (string, optional), `rating` (1-5, optional — a random one is used if missing).\n\n**Tools the agent can choose:** `Wikipedia Search` for general background, `knowledge_base` for the course's own policies. Memory keeps the last 10 turns per `conversation_id`, so two calls with the same id share context.\n\n**Output:** the agent's answer plus `overall_status` (`excellent` or `needs_improvement`). Low ratings produce a `logged_row` you would append to Google Sheets or a database in production.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 420
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ai-agent-review-trigger",
      "name": "AI Agent Review Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "ai-agent-review",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "prepare-request",
      "name": "Prepare Request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        480,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "user_request",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.request }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "conversation_id",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.conversation_id || 'default-session' }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "support-agent",
      "name": "Support Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        740,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.user_request }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a support assistant for an online course. Use the knowledge_base tool for questions about the course's policies and Wikipedia Search for general background. Always say which tools you used. If neither tool has the answer, say so."
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "id": "openai-chat-model",
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        520,
        780
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "simple-memory",
      "name": "Simple Memory",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.memoryBufferWindow",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        680,
        780
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "sessionIdType": "customKey",
        "sessionKey": "={{ $json.conversation_id }}",
        "contextWindowLength": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "wikipedia-search",
      "name": "Wikipedia Search",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequestTool",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        840,
        780
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "action",
              "value": "query"
            },
            {
              "name": "list",
              "value": "search"
            },
            {
              "name": "srsearch",
              "value": "={{ $fromAI('search_term', 'The topic to look up on Wikipedia, in a few words', 'string') }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "format",
              "value": "json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {},
        "toolDescription": "Searches Wikipedia for background information on a topic."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-tool",
      "name": "Knowledge Base Tool",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.vectorStoreInMemory",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1000,
        780
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "retrieve-as-tool",
        "toolName": "knowledge_base",
        "toolDescription": "Searches the course's own knowledge base (refunds, access, certificates, support). Use it for any question about the course's policies.",
        "memoryKey": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "course_knowledge_base"
        },
        "topK": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "openai-embeddings",
      "name": "Embeddings OpenAI",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.embeddingsOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1000,
        1000
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": "text-embedding-3-small",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "capture-rating",
      "name": "Capture Rating",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1080,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "synthesis_answer",
              "value": "={{ $json.output }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "rating",
              "value": "={{ Number($('AI Agent Review Trigger').item.json.body.rating) || (Math.floor(Math.random() * 5) + 1) }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rating-good",
      "name": "Rating Good?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1320,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.rating }}",
              "rightValue": 4,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gte"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "good-no-action-needed",
      "name": "Good - No Action Needed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1560,
        320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "overall_status",
              "value": "excellent"
            },
            {
              "name": "feedback_note",
              "value": "Rating was 4 or higher — no logging needed."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "log-low-rating-simulated",
      "name": "Log Low Rating (Simulated)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1560,
        540
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "overall_status",
              "value": "needs_improvement"
            },
            {
              "name": "logged_row",
              "value": "={{ { timestamp: $now.toISO(), rating: $json.rating, user_request: $('Prepare Request').item.json.user_request, synthesis_answer: $json.synthesis_answer } }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "note",
              "value": "In production this would append to Google Sheets or a database — simulated here as a Set node per Day 40's pattern."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "build-error-response",
      "name": "Build Error Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1080,
        640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "overall_status",
              "value": "error"
            },
            {
              "name": "error_response",
              "value": "Sorry — the assistant couldn't finish that request. Please try again in a minute."
            },
            {
              "name": "error_detail",
              "value": "={{ $json.error?.message || JSON.stringify($json.error || $json) }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
